  "scope": "Local macOS arm64 signed control multiplexing and owned cleanup. Native offer/answer and media remain open. No external crate, package, remote/Linux, performance, whole-task or acceptance qualification.",
  "implementation": [
    "One owned SDK driver correlates interleaved signed reply batches by envelope ID and exact scope. It reuses canonical correlation, step-up, frame/byte and absolute authority/deadline checks.",
    "One shared bound of16 covers queued and active exchanges. Callers waiting for capacity can cancel or expire without submission. Per-exchange batch bounds remain128frames/2MiB; owned signaling and unmatched event inboxes retain their existing bounds.",
    "Submitted exchanges remain owned after local caller cancellation. Status and durable decisions can complete while another reply is pending. There are no automatic mutation retries.",
    "Explicit close, invalid correlation/scope or incomplete exchange deadline retires the peer, preserves submitted mutation keys and drains unwritten commands. Reader shutdown is joined; close retains timeout/cancellation joinability."
  ],
